<article class="env-lemma" id="0DUD">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DUD">Lemma <span data-tag="0DUD">101.45.7</span>.</a> Let $f : \mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{Y}$ be a morphism of algebraic stacks. Assume $f$ is étale, $f$ induces an isomorphism between automorphism groups at points (Remark <a href="/tag/0DTW" data-tag="0DTW">101.19.5</a>), and for every algebraically closed field $k$ the functor </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  f : \mathop{\mathrm{Mor}}\nolimits (\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k), \mathcal{X}) \longrightarrow \mathop{\mathrm{Mor}}\nolimits (\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k), \mathcal{Y})  \]
</div>
  <p> is an equivalence. Then $f$ is an isomorphism. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/0CPN" data-tag="0CPN">101.14.5</a> we see that $f$ is universally injective. Combining Lemmas <a href="/tag/0DU7" data-tag="0DU7">101.45.1</a> and <a href="/tag/0DU9" data-tag="0DU9">101.45.3</a> we see that $f$ is representable by algebraic spaces. Hence $f$ is an open immersion by Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/05W5" data-tag="05W5">67.51.2</a>. To finish we remark that the condition in the lemma also guarantees that $f$ is surjective. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>